WebKit itself is not copied here: recipes/fetch_sources.sh fetches the WPE WebKit 2.54.1 release (and the curl network
backend of the same tag from WebKit's git repository), pinned by SHA-256 and commit in sources.lock and webkit.lock, and
apply_patches.sh / patch.py edit that tree and add our files to it. WebKit is copyright Apple Inc. and the other WebKit
contributors, under the GNU Lesser General Public License 2.1 (WebCore, JavaScriptCore, parts of WTF; LICENSES/LGPL-2.1.txt)
and a BSD 2-clause licence (Apple's files, WTF, bmalloc; LICENSES/WebKit-Apple-BSD-2-Clause.txt). The engine is built
into separate DLLs (browserengine.dll, and the test executables) and never linked into other components, so that the LGPL's
relinking right holds: build.sh leaves the engine's archives in $PHOREPOC_BUILD/thirdparty/*/cxxrt/web/, and the registry
entries link them, so a modified WebKit can be relinked into the same DLL.

Files in os/src/webkit/phwebview adapted from WebKit files (PhDatabaseProvider.*, from WebKitLegacy's
WebDatabaseProvider.*, and PhIDBServer.*, from InProcessIDBServer.*) keep their original notices (Apple Inc., BSD
2-clause). Other files of the port implement WebCore interfaces and follow the structure of WebKit files they stand in
for (PhPlatformStrategies.cpp, ResourceHandleSymbian.cpp, the *MbedTLS.cpp alternatives of the curl backend's TLS helpers,
the Symbian seams in os/src/webkit/symbian); where code is copied from WebKit (OpenSSLHelperMbedTLS.cpp copies one helper
of OpenSSLHelper.cpp, Sony Interactive Entertainment, BSD 2-clause) it stays under WebKit's licence.

